            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"REFINED\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"The transcendent dwelling place of God, the center of His divine authority (throne), and the ultimate eternal destination or abode of the redeemed.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"The jurisdiction where God's will is perfectly executed, encompassing both the visible sky and His seat of rule, characterized by a downward movement of salvation to earth.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"God's transcendent dwelling place and the eternal destiny of believers.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"The jurisdiction of God's realized will and seat of rule, which initiates downward saving action toward earth.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"COMPATIBLE_OVERLAP\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"PARTIAL_RECLASSIFICATION\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The book excludes the popular emphasis on heaven as an upward 'final destination' for believers, instead emphasizing it as the starting point for salvation's downward movement to earth. It also conceptually unites the 'visible sky' and the 'seat of rule' under a single functional definition of jurisdiction.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"The book shifts the primary spatial vector of salvation from upward (believers going to heaven, the consensus primary meaning) to downward (heaven/salvation coming to earth), though this downward movement is noted in consensus alternatives (e.g., N.T. Wright's new creation emphasis).\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The book retains the consensus understanding of heaven as God's seat of rule and authority, but refines the concept by defining it functionally (where God's will is done) and reorienting its eschatological vector (downward to earth rather than an upward afterlife destination).\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"STRONG\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"By framing heaven strictly as a jurisdiction from which salvation descends, the entry neglects numerous New Testament texts that speak of heaven as an inheritance, a reward, and a place believers go to dwell with Christ.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
